{
  "sentences": [
    {
      "id": 56,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "«Pero, Holmes,"},
        {"t": [2, 3, 4, 5], "es": "¿qué hay de la bicicleta?»,"}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "pero"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "Holmes"},
        {"t": [2, 3], "es": "qué hay de", "base": "what about", "sense": "consider", "note": "Sirve para recordar algo que no se ha tenido en cuenta: «¿y qué pasa con…?» No se traduce palabra por palabra."},
        {"t": [4, 5], "es": "la bicicleta", "base": "bicycle", "sense": "vehicle"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 57,
      "line": [{"t": [0, 1], "es": "pregunté."}],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "yo"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "pregunté", "base": "ask", "sense": "question"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 58,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "«Sí, Watson,"},
        {"t": [2, 3, 4, 5, 6], "es": "no debemos olvidar la bicicleta,"},
        {"t": [7, 8], "es": "por supuesto."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "sí", "base": "yes", "sense": "agreement"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "Watson"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "tenemos que recordar", "base": "remember", "sense": "recall", "note": "El modal *must* expresa necesidad y va con el verbo sin *to* ([[modal-verbs]]). Aquí equivale a «no debemos olvidar»."},
        {"t": [5, 6], "es": "la bicicleta", "base": "bicycle", "sense": "vehicle"},
        {"t": [7, 8], "es": "por supuesto", "base": "of course", "sense": "obvious", "note": "Es una expresión fija: no habla de un «curso»."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 59,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "Pero antes,"},
        {"t": [2, 3], "es": "miremos"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6], "es": "hacia el sur"},
        {"t": [7, 8, 9], "es": "y el norte."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "pero"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "primero", "base": "first", "sense": "order"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "vamos a", "base": "let", "sense": "suggest", "note": "*Let’s* es *let us*, pero sirve para proponer algo que haremos juntos: «vamos a…» ([[contractions]])."},
        {"t": [3], "es": "mirar", "base": "look", "sense": "see"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6], "es": "hacia el sur", "base": "south", "sense": "direction"},
        {"t": [7], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [8, 9], "es": "el norte", "base": "north", "sense": "direction"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 60,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Al sur"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6, 7], "es": "tenemos un río grande,"},
        {"t": [9, 10, 11, 12], "es": "así que por ahí no se puede ir en bicicleta."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "al sur", "base": "south", "sense": "direction"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "tenemos", "base": "have", "sense": "possess"},
        {"t": [5, 7], "es": "un río", "base": "river", "sense": "water"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "grande", "base": "big", "sense": "size"},
        {"t": [9, 10], "es": "no hay bicicletas", "base": "bicycle", "sense": "vehicle", "note": "*No* delante de un nombre significa «ningún» ([[negative-words]]). Aquí se sobreentiende que no se puede ir en bicicleta."},
        {"t": [11], "es": "allí, por ahí", "base": "there", "sense": "place"},
        {"t": [12], "es": "por tanto, entonces", "base": "then", "sense": "inference", "note": "Aquí introduce una conclusión, no un momento en el tiempo."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 61,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "Y al norte"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10], "es": "tenemos el bosquecillo llamado Ragged Shaw,"},
        {"t": [11, 12], "es": "y después"},
        {"t": [13, 14, 15], "es": "un gran páramo,"},
        {"t": [16, 17, 18, 19], "es": "el páramo de Lower Gill."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [1, 2, 3], "es": "al norte", "base": "north", "sense": "direction"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [5], "es": "tenemos", "base": "have", "sense": "possess"},
        {"t": [6, 7], "es": "los árboles", "base": "tree", "sense": "plant", "note": "Aquí, *the trees* se refiere a un bosquecillo: un grupo pequeño de árboles."},
        {"t": [8], "es": "llamados", "base": "call", "sense": "name", "note": "*Called* seguido de un nombre indica cómo se llama algo."},
        {"t": [9, 10], "es": "Ragged Shaw", "note": "*Shaw* es una palabra antigua para un bosquecillo; *ragged* significa «irregular, desigual»."},
        {"t": [11], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [12], "es": "después", "base": "then", "sense": "next"},
        {"t": [13, 15], "es": "un páramo", "base": "moor", "sense": "land", "note": "Terreno alto y abierto, sin árboles, típico del norte de Inglaterra."},
        {"t": [14], "es": "grande", "base": "great", "sense": "large"},
        {"t": [16, 17, 18, 19], "es": "el páramo de Lower Gill", "base": "moor", "sense": "land"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 62,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], "es": "Y aquí está Holdernesse Hall,"},
        {"t": [5, 6, 7, 8, 9], "es": "a dieciséis kilómetros del colegio"},
        {"t": [10, 11], "es": "por carretera,"},
        {"t": [12, 13, 14, 15], "es": "pero a solo nueve kilómetros"},
        {"t": [16, 17, 18], "es": "a través del páramo."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "aquí", "base": "here", "sense": "place"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "está", "base": "be", "sense": "state"},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "Holdernesse Hall", "base": "hall", "sense": "house", "note": "En el nombre de una casa, *Hall* indica una gran casa de campo."},
        {"t": [5], "es": "dieciséis"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "kilómetros", "base": "kilometre", "sense": "distance", "note": "Ortografía británica; en EE. UU., *kilometers* ([[british-american]])."},
        {"t": [7, 8, 9], "es": "del colegio", "base": "school", "sense": "education"},
        {"t": [10, 11], "es": "por carretera", "base": "road", "sense": "route"},
        {"t": [12], "es": "pero"},
        {"t": [13], "es": "solo", "base": "only", "sense": "just"},
        {"t": [14], "es": "nueve"},
        {"t": [15], "es": "kilómetros", "base": "kilometre", "sense": "distance", "note": "Ortografía británica; en EE. UU., *kilometers* ([[british-american]])."},
        {"t": [16, 17, 18], "es": "a través del páramo", "base": "moor", "sense": "land"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 63,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "No hay más casas"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6, 7], "es": "hasta la posada Green Man,"},
        {"t": [8, 9, 10, 11], "es": "por la carretera de Chesterfield»."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 2], "es": "no hay casas", "base": "house", "sense": "building", "note": "*No* delante del nombre ya expresa la negación ([[negative-words]]). Aquí equivale a «no hay»."},
        {"t": [1], "es": "otras", "base": "other", "sense": "different"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6, 7], "es": "hasta la posada Green Man", "base": "inn", "sense": "lodging", "note": "*Green Man* significa «el hombre verde», una figura del folclore inglés. Es un nombre habitual de posadas."},
        {"t": [8, 9, 11], "es": "por la carretera", "base": "road", "sense": "route"},
        {"t": [10], "es": "de Chesterfield", "note": "*Chesterfield* describe a qué lugar lleva la carretera; va antes de *road* ([[noun-as-adjective]])."}
      ]
    },
    {
